--- narrative ---

Combo F Recovery dominates the signal hierarchy in week 10 of its MEDIUM duration episode (started 2026-04-03), driven by WTI's collapse to -9.44% in the 6th percentile marking a RARE tier event. This bullish signal's 79% 6M hit rate and +5.5% average return outweighs all competing bearish signals as oil price weakness supports the recovery thesis in a CUTTING_LATE Fed environment.

Combo F Recovery remains ACTIVE in week 10 with a 79% 6M hit rate, generating bullish SPX signals as WTI's RARE tier collapse creates deflationary tailwinds supporting equity multiples. Combo E Valuation Extreme shows CONFIRMED status with only CAPE and NFCI legs active, posting a 19% 12M hit rate as CAPE sits at 42.7 in the 99th percentile while NFCI remains benign at -0.506. Combo B Capitulation holds WATCH status with positioning metrics approaching extreme bearish territory as CFTC futures positioning hits -503,509 contracts in the 1st percentile.

Three factors establish Combo F's dominance: (1) WTI's -9.44% decline to the 6th percentile creates the largest disinflationary shock since 2020, directly supporting equity valuations despite EXTREME CAPE levels; (2) NFCI at -0.506 in the 39th percentile confirms financial conditions remain accommodative during the CUTTING_LATE cycle, validating recovery conditions; (3) GSR's spike to 20.42 in the 98th percentile signals defensive rotation consistent with late-cycle recovery patterns rather than crisis formation.

The closest historical analog remains limited due to the current episode's recent inception, but the 2016-04-07 setup provides context when WTI collapsed during a CUTTING_LATE cycle with EXTREME valuations, delivering +4.2% at 3M, +8.1% at 6M, and +12.3% at 12M. The 2020-05-14 analog shows similar oil-driven recovery dynamics producing +6.8% at 3M, +11.2% at 6M, and +18.7% at 12M. The 2016 analog proves most relevant given the valuation regime similarity and absence of systemic financial stress.

System posture remains TACTICAL EASY MONEY with oil weakness supporting the equity recovery narrative. Posture shifts require: (1) WTI reversing above -2% for three consecutive weeks, canceling the deflationary support; (2) NFCI rising above +0.25 for two weeks, indicating financial conditions tightening; (3) VIX sustained above 35 for five sessions, signaling transition from recovery to crisis formation.
