--- narrative ---

Combo F (Recovery) dominates the signal hierarchy in week 10 of its MEDIUM duration episode, driven by WTI crude collapsing to the 1st percentile at -13.7% annual change. This recovery signal maintains a 79% 6M hit rate and overrides the confirmed Combo E Valuation Extreme on priority ranking and horizon alignment.

Combo F Recovery remains ACTIVE since April 3, 2026, with its bullish SPX signal showing 79% 6M hit rate and +5.5% average returns driven by WTI's extreme 1st percentile collapse providing the primary momentum catalyst. Combo E Valuation Extreme stands CONFIRMED with CAPE and NFCI legs active, delivering a bearish 12M signal with 19% hit rate but +10.9% average returns when successful, as CAPE sits at the 99th percentile at 42.7 and NFCI normalizes at the 39th percentile. Combo B Capitulation maintains WATCH status with no current signal generation.

The dominant Recovery signal wins on three factors: (1) WTI's 1st percentile collapse at -13.7% creates the primary deflationary impulse that historically drives risk asset rebounds within 6M horizons, (2) the CUTTING_LATE Fed cycle regime provides monetary accommodation with the yield curve STEEPENING at 42bp supporting duration rallies, and (3) GLOBAL_EASY liquidity conditions with NFCI at -0.506 override the EXTREME valuation headwinds from CAPE's 99th percentile reading in medium-term tactical windows.

Historical analogs remain incomplete due to recent episode initiation, but the current setup mirrors early 2016 oil crash recovery dynamics when WTI collapsed 70% before Fed accommodation drove 6M equity rallies exceeding 8%. The March 2020 scenario provides a closer analog where extreme energy deflation combined with Fed easing generated 15% SPX returns over 6M despite initial valuation concerns. The 2008 analog diverges due to credit system stress absent in current NFCI readings.

System posture remains TACTICAL EASY MONEY based on Recovery signal dominance and accommodative regime overlay. Posture shifts require: (1) WTI rising above the 25th percentile for two consecutive weeks canceling the energy deflation catalyst, (2) NFCI rising above +0.5 indicating liquidity tightening, or (3) VIX exceeding 35 for five trading days signaling systemic stress overwhelming the recovery narrative.
