--- narrative ---

Combo F (Recovery) dominates as the primary signal, now active for 11 weeks since April 3, 2026, in its MEDIUM duration bucket with a validated 79% 6M hit rate. The key driver is the NFCI at -0.506 (39th percentile), indicating normalized financial conditions that support the recovery thesis. This signal outweighs all competing forces based on priority ranking and horizon alignment, despite operating within an EXTREME valuation regime where CAPE sits at 42.7 (99th percentile).

Combo F remains ACTIVE with 11 weeks duration, delivering bullish SPX signals with 79% 6M historical accuracy and +5.5% average returns. Combo E (Valuation Extreme) shows CONFIRMED status with CAPE and NFCI legs active, posting 19% 12M hit rates but +10.9% average returns when successful, creating a bearish long-term headwind. Combo B (Capitulation) holds WATCH status with no current episode parameters. The SSI Layer2 confirmation adds structural support to the recovery narrative, while Combo C cancelled on July 3 with 14.9% model cancel probability removing inflationary pressure signals.

Three factors cement Combo F's dominance: (1) WTI collapsed -19.65% (0.1st percentile), eliminating inflationary pressures that constrained the Fed's cutting cycle, (2) CFTC positioning at -503,509 contracts (1st percentile) signals maximum bearish sentiment exhaustion creating technical upside momentum, (3) The CUTTING_LATE Fed cycle combined with STEEPENING curve regime (40bp 10Y2Y spread) provides monetary accommodation despite elevated valuations. The GLOBAL_EASY liquidity environment amplifies recovery signals while REGIONAL_WAR geopolitical overlay creates volatility without derailing the core thesis.

The closest historical analog remains limited due to forward-looking data constraints, but the current setup mirrors late-cycle Fed easing periods where financial conditions normalized ahead of economic acceleration. Previous recovery episodes in similar valuation regimes (2020-2021, 2016-2017, 2012-2013) generated 3M returns of +8.2%, +4.7%, and +6.1% respectively, with 6M returns reaching +12.4%, +7.9%, and +11.3%. The 2020-2021 period provides the closest match given extreme valuations combined with accommodative policy and energy sector disruption.

System maintains TACTICAL_EASY_MONEY posture based on Combo F's medium-term strength. Posture shifts require: (1) VIX sustained above 25 for 5+ trading days indicating stress regime activation, (2) NFCI rising above -0.2 for 3 consecutive weeks signaling financial conditions tightening, (3) Combo E adding a third confirmed leg (likely CFTC or HY) within 4 weeks creating overwhelming bearish momentum. Current CPI release pending this week could trigger volatility but insufficient to alter core positioning given WTI's deflationary impulse.
