WTI crude has collapsed -22.1% in 4 weeks (1th percentile) — the sharpest oil drop in years — removing the stagflation pressure that previously activated Combo C. This disinflationary impulse reduces the CPI risk leg and gives the Fed room to ease further. CAPE at 41.9x (99th percentile) has confirmed Combo E (Valuation Extreme, CONFIRMED (legs: CAPE, NFCI), 18.9% (12M)). However, Combo E operates on a 12m horizon — a slow structural headwind, not a near-term catalyst. It does not override Combo F's momentum at week 12. VXTS (VIX term structure) at 1.10 flags mild complacency — near-term options are unusually cheap relative to the 3-month outlook. This keeps Combo D (FOMO Top) partially elevated but CFTC positioning at 1th percentile is far too short to confirm the crowding leg, so Combo D remains on WATCH only.

Competing signals: Combo B (Capitulation) is on WATCH (bullish); not yet firing. Combo C (Stagflation / Energy Shock) has been CANCELLED. Combo E (Valuation Extreme) is CONFIRMED (bearish, 18.9% (12M)).

System posture: TACTICAL EASY MONEY. A CPI release is pending this week — a hot surprise above +0.2pp would re-activate the Combo C inflation leg and shift posture. SSI Layer 2 is CONFIRMED, applying a 1.20x multiplier to position sizing.
