--- narrative ---

Combo F (Recovery) is the dominant signal, active for week 12 of 26 (started 2026-04-03), 14 weeks remaining in active window. Its validated 6M hit rate is 79% 6M (+5.5% avg), making it the highest-confidence signal in the current stack. Hedge fund positioning (CFTC Fast Money net -523,882 contracts, 1th percentile) remains extremely short, providing structural fuel for the recovery — the covering rally has not yet run its full course. The macro backdrop — CUTTING_LATE Fed cycle with steepening yield curve and GLOBAL_EASY global liquidity — is broadly supportive of the dominant bullish signal. 

WTI crude has collapsed -19.6% in 4 weeks (1th percentile) — the sharpest oil drop in years — removing the stagflation pressure that previously activated Combo C. This disinflationary impulse reduces the CPI risk leg and gives the Fed room to ease further. CAPE at 41.0x (99th percentile) has confirmed Combo E (Valuation Extreme, CONFIRMED (legs: CAPE, NFCI), 18.9% (12M)). However, Combo E operates on a 12m horizon — a slow structural headwind, not a near-term catalyst. It does not override Combo F's momentum at week 12.

Competing signals: Combo C (Stagflation / Energy Shock) has been CANCELLED. Combo E (Valuation Extreme) is CONFIRMED (bearish, 18.9% (12M)).

System posture: TACTICAL EASY MONEY. A CPI release is pending this week — a hot surprise above +0.2pp would re-activate the Combo C inflation leg and shift posture. SSI Layer 2 is CONFIRMED, applying a 1.20x multiplier to position sizing.
